findings.description:
Description: The slice design's data flow places the detached-HEAD check first in the precondition stage ("identify_operator → branch_exists → sha compare", all before the model call), and D2 states "a detached HEAD refuses before either check." Task 3.1 (line 79) correctly makes `current_branch` raise for detached HEAD, but no task wires `current_branch` into the command's precondition order, and no task-level test covers the command-level refusal:
- Task 13.1 (line 298) names the order as "preconditions (identity, then pushed)" with no detached-HEAD term;
- Task 13.2 (line 309) has no detached-HEAD case (its identity-refusal case covers the "no login" criterion, but nothing covers the head-refusal);
- Task 14.1 lists the five call sites and is not where it belongs either.

Task 3.2's unit test only proves the helper raises — the end-to-end outcome (command exits non-zero, names the condition, makes no write, calls the composer never) is the form every other refusal in this slice is tested at the command level. As written, whether `current_branch` is called before `identify_operator`, its exception is converted to an exit-1 refusal rather than an unhandled traceback, and no host call fires are all left to implementation judgment. Fix: add a detached-HEAD term to Task 13.1's order and one refusal case to Task 13.2 (mirroring the identity-refusal case).
